-- Are the indicators reported for the timestep that produced them, or summed
-- over the report interval?  Everything below happens inside a single ten day
-- report step, with timesteps capped at one day.
--
--   B-1H  CECON closes two connections on the first timestep.
--   B-2H  ACTIONX tightens WECON at TIME > 5, closing connections much later
--         in the same report interval.
--
-- Per timestep, each event appears on its own ministep row and the day ten
-- report row is zero for both wells.  Per report interval, the day ten row
-- carries both.  The value that matters is therefore which row it lands on,
-- not the count.  Do not add RPTONLY or summary thinning to this deck: they
-- discard the ministep rows the comparison needs.

INCLUDE
 'include/wpwe-model.inc' /

SUMMARY
INCLUDE
 'include/wpwe-summary.inc' /

SCHEDULE
TUNING
 0.1 1.0 1.0e-4 /
 /
 /

INCLUDE
 'include/wpwe-wells.inc' /

CECON
 'B-1H' 2* 3 4 1* 1.0 1* 'CON' /
/

ACTIONX
 'LATECON' 1 /
 TIME > 5 /
/
WECON
 'B-2H' 3* 1.0 1* 'CON' /
/
ENDACTIO

TSTEP
 10 /

TSTEP
 2 /
END
